{
  "name": "Driver COD Briefing",
  "description": "Weekday mornings at 9am Edmonton (Mon-Fri, no weekends): calls the RxDeliver driverCodBriefing function which pushes each driver with outstanding uncollected CODs a notification listing their CODs, then the agent composes and sends the app owner a full briefing broken down by driver.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 9 * * 1-5",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "America/Edmonton",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "driver_cod_briefing",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.0.4"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "run_and_report": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "It is 9am \u2014 the weekday driver COD briefing is running now (Mon-Fri only; no briefing on weekends). Follow these steps exactly:\n\n1. Run this bash command (it triggers the RxDeliver briefing function, which sends push notifications to every driver with outstanding uncollected CODs and returns the full grouped JSON):\ncurl -s -X POST 'https://base44.app/api/apps/68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6/functions/driverCodBriefing' -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BASE44_SERVICE_TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n\n2. From the returned JSON, compose a compact app-owner briefing in PLAIN TEXT (WhatsApp, no markdown) broken down BY DRIVER. Match the Square Catalog item format exactly \u2014 the MONEY comes FIRST on each item line:\n\nROBERT T \u2014 2 CODs, $ 204.76\n$ 200.02 \u00b7 09/03(HS)-Glenn Bursey\n$   4.74 \u00b7 09/14(LD)-Jeanne Lavallee\n\nLAYOUT RULES: within each driver block, right-align the money column \u2014 pad every item amount (and the driver header total) to the same width so all $ signs and decimals line up vertically. Each item line = '$ ' + right-padded amount + ' \u00b7 ' + MM/DD delivery date + '(' + store abbreviation + ')' + '-' + patient name. Header line = DRIVER NAME \u2014 N CODs, $ + total.\nAfter all driver blocks, end with: OVERALL TOTAL: N CODs, $ X.XX\nThen note push delivery failures briefly (from the pushes array: sent/skipped/errors per driver) \u2014 e.g. 'Push delivery failures: none reported.'\nIf there are no outstanding CODs, just say the COD slate is clean.\n\n3. Broadcast the briefing to the owner via broadcast_message, then stop."
          },
          "x-base44": {
            "description": "Push driver COD notifications, brief the owner",
            "title": "Driver COD briefing"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}